    "sectionNumber": 208,
    "chapter": "CHAPTER XII",
    "chapterTitle": "Municipal Properties, Fisheries, Payao & Public Market Stalls",
    "title": "Surcharge for late or non-payment of fees.",
    "fullText": "a) Surcharge for late or non-payment of fees. The lessee of a stall, who fails to pay the monthly \nrental fee within the prescribed period, shall pay a surcharge of twenty-five percent (25%) of the \ntotal rent due. \n\nFailure to pay the rental for three (3) consecutive months shall cause automatic cancellation of the \ncontract of lease or stall prejudice to suing the lessee for the unpaid rents at the expense of the \nlessee. The stall shall be declared vacant and subject to adjudication. \n\nb) Any person occupying more space that what is duly leased him shall pay double the regular \nrate for such extra space and any person who fails to pay the monthly rent within the time fixed \nherein shall pay a penalty of twenty-five percent (25%) of the rent due. The lease contract of any \nperson found habitually incurring the foregoing violation shall be cancelled. \n\nc) Any person occupying space in the market premises without first paying the fee imposed in this \nArticle shall pay three (3) times as much as the regular rate for the space occupied.",
